{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/211330-dark-ages-delhi-an-open-call-for-help","id":211330,"title":"Dark Ages: Delhi: an open call for help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-28T09:43:11-07:00","id":211330,"title":"Dark Ages: Delhi: an open call for help","content":"Hello all! I'm Alqamar Alaswad; some of you may remember me from the Shadownessence forums, where I was very active during some years, when I was working on the Fomorian Project. Well, the project is still going on, I'm using on my Changeling: the Dreaming games, etc...<br /> <br /> But that is not the reason I am here this evening.<br /> <br /> I am here because I am going to GM a short-chronicle called &quot;Where the Black Lotus blooms&quot;. Using Dark Ages: Vampire, Veil of Night and Blood and Silk as my main rulebooks. The game is going to take place In Delhi, which is mainly Mehrauli at that time (1230). Basically, it is a simple tale about a group of Western Cainities being sent by their sires, a dark, devious group \u00e0 la 'Conspiracy of Isaac' (Giovanni Chronicles), to contact the Cainites living in Delhi and to come back with a mythical plant called 'The Black Lotus', a narcotic flower the petals of which are rumored to be able to quench the thirst of any Cainite. They are given letters of presentation for both the Ashirra and the Hindu Cainites that call the city their home.<br /> <br /> When they get there they are going to fall right in the middle of a three-sided war between the Ashirra, the court of the Hindu Cainites (the Ravnos and their allies) and the asuratziyya, the region's native Cathayans, who are... mainly followers of the Flame of the Rising Phoenix.<br /> <br /> So, this is an open call for help. All ideas are welcome.<br /> <br /> What kind of reference materials would you use? What kind of music? What rulebooks? What would you like to see if you were playing in a game such as this? What would you hate to see? Why? Why not? Last, but not least, have you got any other kind of help you would like to share with me?<br /> <br /> Thanks for all your help. The game begins on Saturday, August the 2nd, and I will post here information about my players and their actions as the game progresses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 07-28-2014, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T11:53:55-07:00","id":211515,"title":"","content":"you could make a whole chronicle out of the journey itself already...<br /> <br /> Some things which for your world travelling cainites should be obvious are such as; the notable wealth of the city and its astounding smiths whose swords make the famed damask-smiths cry in shame not to mention the iron pillar of Delhi and other monuments dotting the city. Never before seen spices and drinks (for ghoul retinue) high learning among the upper castes and the complete opposite among the lower caste. Also the segregation of society is strict even by medieval European standards -there's no moving between castes EVER and marrying to wrong cast was punishable by death. The land is just filled with Asian shapechangers -until 19th century and the coming of the Brits all lands between Mesopotamia and Siam peninsula were quite wild and literal tiger country.<br /> <br /> There's more ofc but you should get a few history books to read to get the idea of what medieval Indian society was like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T12:14:44-07:00","id":211546,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your comments.<br /> I'm using John Keay's India as my main source for real world info.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T17:54:26-07:00","id":211866,"title":"","content":"I'd swap the major Cathayan antagonists with Face of the Gods, since they are more common around there but also because really they are so perfect for antagonists(&quot;wait they think they are gods?&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T18:37:44-07:00","id":211894,"title":"","content":"In &quot;Wraith, the Oblivion: Wraith Play